{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:cdbf34043baceb78","name":"Fighting Space","source":{"id":"source:reference-cdbf34043baceb78","title":"Fighting Space","revision":26700,"timestamp":"2025-06-05T01:22:41Z","sha256":"cdba7cb0e2ce65c7c9bab858282e4b8c437a8608969adcd87a205b7bc07a1f4c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=26700","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Fighting%20Space&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-cdbf34043baceb78","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The squares that a creature occupies on the Battle Map are collectively referred to as its Fighting Space. Small and Medium creatures (including most characters) have a Fighting Space of 1 square. Large creatures have a Fighting Space of 4 squares (2 squares on a side). Huge creatures have a Fighting Space of 9 squares (3 squares on a side). Gargantuan and Colossal creatures have much larger Fighting Spaces.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EXAMPLE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["REFLEX"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/REFLEX"}," MODIFIER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["FIGHTING SPACE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Fine\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Insect\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["<1 Square\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Diminutive\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Grenade"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grenade"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["<1 Square\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Tiny\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Mouse Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mouse_Droid"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["<1 Square\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Small\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Jawa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jawa","referenceId":"reference:0b0fb3f831db6b3c"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1 Square\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Medium\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1 Square\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Speeder Bike\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2x2 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Huge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Landspeeder\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3x3 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["ARC-170 Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/ARC-170_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:fd7701de3a3d42d7"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4x4 Squares\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6x6+ Squares\n"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike Character Combat, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," allows a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," to move into a square with another ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"},". A square can hold up to two ground ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," and two flying ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"}," at a time. There are no direct consequences for moving past, into, or out of a square already occupied by a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," (though occupying the same square might allow the enemy to target you with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attacks"},").\n"]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Reach"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A creature's Reach determines the distance it can Reach when making a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"},". A creature Threatens all squares within its Reach. Small and Medium characters have a Reach of 1 square, which means they can make melee attacks only against targets in adjacent squares. Larger creatures tend to have a greater Reach and, respectively, a bigger Threatened Area.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A creature with greater-than-normal Reach (more than 1 square) can still attack opponents directly next to it. A creature with greater than normal Reach usually receives an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attack of Opportunity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_of_Opportunity"}," against an opponent when the opponent approaches it, because the opponent must enter and move within its Threatened Area before making a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Fine, Diminutive, or Tiny creature must be in your space to attack you; moving into your square provokes an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attack of Opportunity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attack_of_Opportunity"},". You can attack into your own space if you need to with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Attack"}," (but not a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ranged Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ranged_Attack"},"), so you can attack very small opponents normally.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Squeezing"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Creatures of Large size and bigger can Squeeze through small openings and down narrow hallways that are at least half as wide as their Fighting Space, provided they end their movement in an area that they can normally occupy. Big ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," can't Squeeze at all, unless they can compress their frames to accommodate the tighter space. Creatures of Large size or bigger can't Squeeze past opponents.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
